window.docContents[181].resolve({"/Judgments-and-domains/Static-judgments/#Core-C______--Judgments-and-domains--Static-judgments":{"contents":"The judgment  states that the expression  has type  in the context . Each rule concludes about one constructor of Expr, and a constructor may have several rules, as the call of a name has T-Call, T-CallLib, T-CallThis and T-CallFn. A lambda has no rule of this judgment. The judgment  accepts it at its function type, and accepts any other expression by its type.\n\nThe judgment  holds for the expressions that denote a location, a variable not captured by copy, an unqualified field of this, *e, e.f, e->f, the element e[i] of a vector, an operator[] or a method call whose member returns a reference, and a conditional whose two branches denote locations of one type.\n\nThe judgment  states that the command  is well typed and extends  to , so that a declaration reaches the following commands of the sequence. The result type  of the enclosing body, a function, a member or a lambda, is a parameter of the relation, written  in Lean.\n\n","context":"Core C++\u0009Judgments and domains","header":"2.3. Static judgments","id":"/Judgments-and-domains/Static-judgments/#Core-C______--Judgments-and-domains--Static-judgments"}});